# Survey Setup

This document describes the setup of the survey used to collect human annotations for the thesis.

## Introduction

The following introduction was shown to participants at the start of the survey:

Welcome, and thank you for taking part! You've been invited to a short study that's part of an MSc thesis on language technology in aviation. It only takes around 8–10 minutes.

**What is this research about?**

Modern AI language models (like ChatGPT) are trained mostly on general internet text. Because of that, they don't always handle specialized vocabulary very efficiently. This study aims to help make these models work better and more efficiently for the aviation domain. To do that, we need to know which words in our aviation maintenance dataset are truly aviation-specific, which are general technical terms, and which are everyday language. Your knowledge of the field is exactly what makes this useful. There are no right or wrong answers, just your professional intuition.

**What will you be asked to do?**

You'll see 40 words drawn randomly from our dataset. If a word is unfamiliar or the context is unclear, an example sentence is always shown below the question. For each word, you pick one of four categories:

- **Aviation-specific** — Only used in aviation.
- **Technical** — A term with a technical meaning, shared across multiple fields (e.g. "pressure", "torque").
- **Supportive** — A non-technical word that supports technical communication (e.g. "verify", "perform").
- **Everyday** — A common word with no technical meaning.

If you're unsure between two options, go with your first instinct — that's the most useful answer for us.

**A few practical notes:**

- Your responses are anonymous.
- There is no "correct" answer — we want to capture how people from the field perceive these words.
- The whole survey takes roughly 8–10 minutes.

Thank you for your time and for contributing to this research!

## Question Format

Each question was presented in the following format:

*"The word **[word]** is best placed in the following category:"*

With the following answer options:

- Aviation-specific (only used in aviation)
- Technical (A term with a technical meaning, shared across multiple fields)
- Supportive (A non-technical word that supports technical communication)
- Everyday (a common word)
- I have not seen this word before.

Participants selected one option per word. A fifth option, "I have not seen this word before", was included for cases where the participant was unfamiliar with the term.
